  "full_text": "Fruit. Fruit on the vine with how many grapes per cluster. Toes. Graggle. Grapes are like toes. What? Grapes are like toes. What? So, my corona. God reigns over all. A man's steps are ordained by the Lord. How can a man understand his ways? Stop to think for a moment about the word sovereignty. There's a small word nestled in the heart of the word. Sovereignty means our all-wise, all-knowing God reigns in the realms beyond our comprehension, bringing a plan beyond our ability to alter, hinder, or stop. Let me go further. His plan includes all promotions, demotions. His plan can mean both adversity and prosperity, tragedy, calamity, ecstasy, joy. His plan is at work when we cannot imagine why, because it is so unpleasant, as much as the reason is clear and pleasant. His sovereignty... though it is inscrutable, has dominion over all handicaps, all heartaches, all helpless moments. Even when we cannot explain the reasons, he understands. And when we cannot see the end, he is there nodding. Yes, that's my plan.",
